.TH MY_CNTL 1 "2026-10-06" "mu2e-pcie-utils 9.01.00" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
my_cntl \- raw register and driver test commands for a Mu2e DTC/CFO card
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B my_cntl
.RB [ \-d
.IR dtc ]
.RB [ \-l
.IR loops ]
.RB [ \-t ]
.B read
.I offset
.br
.B my_cntl
.RB [ \-d
.IR dtc ]
.B write
.I offset value
.br
.B my_cntl
.RB [ \-d
.IR dtc ]
.BR start | stop | dump
.br
.B my_cntl
.RB [ \-d
.IR dtc ]
.RB [ \-c
.IR chn ]
.B spy
.RI [ optsmask ]
.br
.B my_cntl
.RB [ \-d
.IR dtc ]
.B hash
.RI [ hostname ]
.br
.B my_cntl
.BR \-h | \-V
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B my_cntl
is the lowest-level userspace tool for the
.BR mu2e (4)
driver.
It talks to
.BI /dev/mu2e N
directly, without constructing a
.B DTC
or
.B DTC_Registers
object, so it never re-initialises the card.
Operations scripts use it for register polling: mu2edaq-operations
.B read_dtc_temps.sh
reads the FPGA die temperature at 0x9010 with it and powers the host
off on over-temperature.
.PP
Commands:
.TP
.BI read " offset"
Open
.BI /dev/mu2e N
read-only and issue
.B M_IOC_REG_ACCESS
with
.I access_type
0 once per loop.
.I offset
is parsed with
.BR strtoul (3)
base 0 and stored in the 16-bit
.I reg_offset
field, so offsets above 0xFFFF are silently truncated.
.TP
.BI write " offset value"
Initialise a
.B mu2edev
handle (opens the node read-write and maps the DMA rings) and call
.BR write_register_checked() ,
which issues
.B M_IOC_REG_ACCESS
with
.I access_type
2 (write, then read back under the driver's readback mutex).
If the read-back differs from the written value it prints
.B "NOTE: Write value mismatch 0x\fIW\fP vs readback 0x\fIR\fP"
\(em normal for self-clearing or read-only bits.
.TP
.BR start ", " stop
Issue
.B M_IOC_TEST_START
/
.B M_IOC_TEST_STOP
with an uninitialised
.B m_ioc_cmd_t
argument.
Legacy XPMON test hooks.
.TP
.B dump
Issue
.BR M_IOC_DUMP ;
the driver writes its DMA ring state to the kernel TRACE buffer
.RI ( /proc/trace/buffer )
or printk, not to stdout.
.TP
.BR spy " [\fIoptsmask\fP]"
Call
.BR mu2edev::spy() ,
printing part of each receive (C2S) buffer of channel
.I chn
until interrupted.
.TP
.BR hash " [\fIhostname\fP]"
Print
.BI "hash: " X
where
.I X
is
.BR mu2e_host_hash() :
the 16-bit TRACE name hash of
.I hostname
(default: this host) in bits 31:16 and
.I dtc
in bits 15:0.
The driver writes the same value to the scratch register 0x9030 when it
allocates the card's DMA memory at probe time, so a register dump
identifies the host and index that loaded it.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-d " dtc"
Device index
.IR N " of " /dev/mu2e N .
Default:
.B DTCLIB_DTC
if set, else 0.
.TP
.BI \-l " loops"
Repeat
.B read
this many times (default 1).
.TP
.B \-t
With
.BR read :
print only the initial value and every change, then a summary.
.TP
.BI \-c " chn"
DMA channel for
.BR spy :
0 = DAQ (ROC data), 1 = DCS.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-?
Print usage to stdout and exit 0.
.TP
.B \-V
Print the RCS revision string and exit 0.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-p " \fIn\fP, " \-m " \fIn\fP, " \-\-mem\-to\-malloc " \fIn\fP"
Accepted and ignored.
.SH OUTPUT FORMAT
.B read
writes one line per loop to stdout, exactly
.B 0x%08x
(eight lowercase hex digits), followed by the line
.BR sts=0 .
The
.B sts=
line contains no
.BR 0x ,
so
.B "my_cntl read 0x9010 | grep 0x"
yields only the value line.
With
.B \-t
the lines are
.BR "initial val: 0x%08x" ,
.BR "val changed from 0x%08x \- new val: 0x%08x" ,
and
.B "value changed %d times"
or
.BR "value did not change during %u loops" .
.PP
.BR write ", " start ", " stop ", " dump
print only
.BR sts=%d .
All
.BR perror (3)
text goes to stderr; on any failure stdout carries no
.B 0x
line.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
Also returned for
.BR \-h ,
for an unknown option (getopt returns
.B ?
and usage is printed), and when no command is given
(prints
.B "Need cmd"
and usage on stdout).
.TP
.B 1
Unknown command; missing operand to
.B read
or
.BR write ;
.BR open (2)
of the node failed
.RB ( read ,
.BR start ,
.BR stop ,
.BR dump ;
message
.BR "open: ..." );
or the
.B M_IOC_REG_ACCESS
ioctl failed during
.B read
(message
.BR "ioctl M_IOC_REG_ACCESS read: ..." ),
or
.B M_IOC_DUMP
failed.
.TP
.B 134
.RB ( SIGABRT )
.B write
or
.B spy
when the node cannot be opened:
.B mu2edev::init()
throws and nothing catches it.
.PP
.B write
does not check the ioctl result: it prints
.B sts=0
and exits 0 even if the register write failed.
.B start
and
.B stop
likewise exit 0 regardless of the ioctl result.
.PP
.B open
fails with
.B EBUSY
when another non-root UID currently holds the card open (see
.BR mu2e (4));
a script running as an unprivileged user can therefore fail while
the DAQ owns the device.
.SH FILES
.TP
.BI /dev/mu2e N
Card device node, N = 0..3.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DTCLIB_DTC
Default device index when
.B \-d
is absent.
.TP
.BR TRACE_NAME ", " TRACE_FILE ", " TRACE_LVLS
TRACE configuration for diagnostic messages.
.SH EXAMPLES
Read the FPGA die temperature code of card 1 and convert it with
the same formula as
.BR CFOandDTC_Registers::ReadFPGATemperature() :
.PP
.EX
code=$(my_cntl \-d 1 read 0x9010 | grep 0x)
python3 \-c "print(($code * 503.975 / 4096) \- 273.15)"
.EE
.PP
Watch the SERDES CDR lock register for changes over 1000 reads:
.PP
.EX
my_cntl \-l 1000 \-t read 0x9140
.EE
.PP
Soft-reset card 0 (destructive \(em interrupts any running partition):
.PP
.EX
my_cntl write 0x9100 0x80000000
my_cntl write 0x9100 0x00000000
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mu2e (4),
.BR DTCRegDump (1),
.BR rocUtil (1),
.BR libDTCInterface (3)
